## Context

The tracking must outlive the initial run. A project skill and a short rule
must steer future agents to the harvester, the schema, the registers and the
arbitrations, without copying the architecture into their permanent context.

## Test

Validate the skill with the skill-creator validator. On three realistic
requests — refresh a country, add a project, check a figure — its path must
preserve history, require the primary source and refuse double counting. The
test does not depend on an exact wording.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Concise project skill, schema references loaded on demand
- [ ] Permanent rule limited to the invariants that prevent a published error
- [ ] Refresh mode, project mode and verification mode documented
- [ ] Dry searches and human arbitrations have a stable location
- [ ] No download, DVC push or publication is implicitly authorized
